1
00:05:10,588 --> 00:05:16,588
Loneliness is much better when you have got someone to share it with.

2
00:10:21,176 --> 00:10:27,176
The Station Agent is a drama, comedy film directed by Tom McCarthy.

3
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:37,764
When his only friend dies, a man born with dwarfism moves to rural New Jersey to live a life of
solitude, only to meet a chatty hot dog vendor and a woman dealing with her own personal loss.

4
00:20:42,352 --> 00:20:48,352
Finbar McBride, played by Peter Dinklage.

5
00:25:52,941 --> 00:25:58,941
Olivia Harris, played by Patricia Clarkson.

6
00:31:03,529 --> 00:31:09,529
Joe Oramas, played by Bobby Cannavale.

7
00:36:14,117 --> 00:36:20,117
Emily, played by Michelle Williams.

8
00:41:24,705 --> 00:41:30,705
Cleo, played by Raven Goodwin.

9
00:46:35,294 --> 00:46:41,294
Henry Styles, played by Paul Benjamin.

10
00:51:45,882 --> 00:51:51,882
The Station Agent is a 2003 American comedy-drama film written and
directed by Tom McCarthy in his directorial debut.

11
00:56:56,470 --> 00:57:02,470
It stars Peter Dinklage as a man who seeks solitude in an abandoned train station
in the Newfoundland section of Jefferson Township, New Jersey.

12
01:02:07,058 --> 01:02:13,058
It also stars Patricia Clarkson, Michelle Williams,
Bobby Cannavale and John Slattery.

13
01:07:17,647 --> 01:07:23,647
For his writing achievement, McCarthy won the BAFTA Award for Best Original Screenplay, the
Independent Spirit Award for Best First Screenplay and the Waldo Salt Screenwriting Award.

14
01:12:28,235 --> 01:12:34,235
The film itself also won the John Cassavetes Award.

15
01:17:38,823 --> 01:17:44,823
The film explores themes of friendship, new jersey, small person.

16
01:22:49,411 --> 01:22:55,411
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
